  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Convert these fractions and mixed numerals to decimals. (They are all recurring decimals.)",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$64\\frac59$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$64.\\dot5$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}64\\frac59&=64+(5\\div9)\\\\64\\frac59&=64.555\\ldots\\\\64\\frac59&=64.\\dot5\\end{aligned}$$\n\nEach digit of the fractional part is 5 with remainder 5.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$78\\frac56$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$78.8\\dot3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}78\\frac56&=78+(5\\div6)\\\\78\\frac56&=78.8333\\ldots\\\\78\\frac56&=78.8\\dot3\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe fractional part starts with 8 tenths and remainder 2; subsequent digits are 3 with remainder 2.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$45\\frac2{11}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$45.\\dot1\\dot8$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}45\\frac2{11}&=45+(2\\div11)\\\\45\\frac2{11}&=45.181818\\ldots\\\\45\\frac2{11}&=45.\\dot1\\dot8\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivision of the fractional part gives digits 1 and 8 with remainders 9 and 2; the cycle repeats.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{11}{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.91\\dot6$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{12}&=11\\div12\\\\\\frac{11}{12}&=0.91666\\ldots\\\\\\frac{11}{12}&=0.91\\dot6\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe first two digits are 9 and 1, with remainders 2 and 8. Every subsequent digit is 6 with remainder 8.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$3\\frac27$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.\\dot2 8571\\dot4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}3\\frac27&=3+(2\\div7)\\\\3\\frac27&=3.285714285714\\ldots\\\\3\\frac27&=3.\\dot2 8571\\dot4\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDivision of the fractional part gives digits 2, 8, 5, 7, 1, 4 with remainders 6, 4, 5, 1, 3, 2. The cycle 285714 repeats.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
